# Lazarus — Docker ignore
#
# IMPORTANT: because `apps/web` depends on `packages/*` through pnpm workspaces,
# the Docker build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT, not the app directory. This
# file therefore must NOT exclude `packages/`, `apps/`, or `services/` — doing so
# silently breaks the workspace build rather than failing loudly.

# ── Local state and caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/out
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.cache
**/.vite
**/.vitest
**/TestResults
**/artifacts
**/bin
**/obj
**/vendor
**/__pycache__
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log

# Version control and CI — present in the root context, never in an image
.git
.git/**
.github
**/.git
**/.git/**

# ── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `.env.example` is the only environment file an image may ever contain.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/secrets
!**/.env.example

# ── Local runtime state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are volumes at runtime, not image content. Keeping them out of the
# context prevents a developer's local data leaking into a published layer.
data
var
storage
tmp
*.pid
*.seed

# ── Editor and OS cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea
.vscode
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Build tooling not needed at runtime ────────────────────────────────────
# `justfile`, CI, and docs are excluded, but README/LICENSE/CHANGELOG are kept
# because images ship them for provenance and licence compliance.
justfile
**/*.csproj.DotSettings.user
**/.devcontainer

# ── Keep these ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Explicitly un-ignored so the rules above can never catch them by accident.
!packages/**
!apps/**
!services/**
!README.md
!LICENSE
!CHANGELOG.md